// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 06-declarations/module_binding_without_initializer_neg_01.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A module-scope `let`/`mut` binding may legally omit its initializer only under
// the definite-assignment rule. That rule is specified but not implemented, so
// the form is refused on the signature rail instead of reaching an unimplemented
// middle-end shape and surfacing as an internal compiler error.
// CHECK: Error [ZOM4087]: definite assignment for this module-scope binding is not supported yet
